[2026-03-14T20:43:42.663Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ERVcquoLeJ2Zqv3Nicn9Ag","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile all the information I've gathered for you.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI've completed a thorough exploration of the Google Flights app in the `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights` directory. Here's everything you requested:\n\n### 1. App Directory Name\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n### 2. DealsSection Component\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/DealsSection.tsx`\n\nThe component:\n- Takes props: `deals` (Deal[]), `loading` (boolean), `originCode` (string | null)\n- Displays deal cards in a responsive grid with `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr))`\n- Shows loading state with 4 skeleton cards\n- Shows empty state message when no deals available\n- Each deal card displays:\n  - Destination code with gradient background\n  - Destination city and country\n  - Travel date range (formatDateRange helper)\n  - Price prominently displayed\n  - Savings percentage (if > 0) with \"↓\" indicator\n- Clicking a deal card navigates to `/results?` page with origin, destination, and date parameters\n- Uses extensive `data-testid` attributes for testing\n\n**Styles:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/DealsSection.css` includes grid layout, card styling with hover effects (box-shadow and translateY), skeleton animations, and empty state styling.\n\n### 3. Tests Documentation for DealsSection\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/docs/tests.md` (lines 1353-1413)\n\nThere are 9 test specifications for DealsSection:\n1. **Display deal cards** - Section displays with multiple deal cards from selected origin\n2. **Card content** - Each card shows destination, dates, price, savings, and gradient\n3. **Card click navigation** - Clicking navigates to results page with proper parameters\n4. **Updates on origin change** - Deals reload when origin airport changes\n5. **Loading state** - Shows skeleton loaders while fetching\n6. **Empty state** - Shows message when no deals available\n7. **Grid layout** - Multiple cards displayed in responsive grid/row layout\n8. **Hover effect** - Cards show visual hover effect (shadow/elevation)\n9. **Savings calculation** - Percentage displayed correctly with visual indicator\n\nAdditional spec:\n10. **Refresh on repeated origin changes** - Handles multiple origin changes correctly\n\n### 4. Playwright Configuration\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/playwright.config.ts`\n\nKey settings:\n- testDir: `./tests`\n- timeout: 60000ms\n- expect timeout: 10000ms\n- fullyParallel: false\n- workers: 1 (sequential execution)\n- Uses Replay.io for recording with chromium executable path\n- baseURL: `http://localhost:8888`\n- WebServer: `netlify dev --port 8888 --functions ./netlify/functions`\n- Reporter: list + JSON output to `test-results/results.json`\n\n### 5. Existing Test Files & Patterns\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/tests/` (24 test files)\n\nKey patterns observed:\n\n**Popular test patterns:**\n- `test.describe('ComponentName', () => { ... })` - describes test suites\n- `test.beforeEach()` - setup before each test\n- `page.goto()` - navigation\n- `page.getByTestId('testid')` - primary locator strategy\n- `await expect(...).toBeVisible({ timeout: 10000 })` - visibility checks\n- `await expect(...).toContainText(...)` - text content verification\n- `toHaveURL(/\\/path\\?/)` - URL pattern matching\n- `toHaveCount()` - for counting elements\n\n**Navigation patterns:**\n- Use URLSearchParams to build query strings\n- Navigate with `page.goto(buildUrl(...))`\n- Extract IDs from `data-testid` attributes to construct new URLs\n\n**Helper functions:**\n- `buildResultsUrl()` - constructs search results URLs with parameters\n- `navigateToBookingPage()` - complex navigation helper\n- `fillSearchForm()` - form interaction helper\n- `deleteAllRecentSearches()` - localStorage manipulation\n\n### 6. Explore Page Component\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/pages/ExplorePage.tsx`\n\nUsage of DealsSection:\n- Imported and used in the explore page at line 16\n- Located in `<section className=\"explore-page__deals-section\">` (lines 87-93)\n- Receives props: `deals`, `loading`, `originCode`\n- Used alongside DestinationMap and FlexibleDatesGrid components\n- Handles fetches via Redux dispatches: `fetchExploreDestinations()` and `fetchExploreDeals()` (lines 34-35)\n\nThe page structure:\n- Origin selector section\n- Map section (DestinationMap)\n- Dates section (FlexibleDatesGrid)\n- Deals section (DealsSection)\n\n### 7. Netlify Functions Related to Deals\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/explore-deals.ts`\n\nFunction details:\n- Endpoint: `/api/explore-deals?origin={originCode}`\n- Query parameter: `origin` (required) - airport IATA code\n- Algorithm:\n  - Finds flights from origin to all destinations in next 90 days\n  - Identifies lowest price flight per destination\n  - Calculates average price per destination for comparison\n  - Selects only flights cheaper than average (discount deals)\n  - Sorts by savings percentage (highest savings first)\n  - Returns max 8 deals\n  - Assumes 1-week return trips (departure_date + 7 days)\n\n- Returns Deal objects with:\n  - `id`, `destination_code`, `destination_city`, `destination_country`\n  - `departure_date`, `return_date`\n  - `price`, `average_price`, `savings_percent`\n  - `gradient` - one of 8 pre-defined gradient strings for UI\n\n**Other related functions:**\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/explore-destinations.ts` - Gets destinations and lowest prices\n- `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/netlify/functions/explore-dates.ts` - Gets date-specific pricing with filtering by range (weekend/1week/2weeks)\n\n**Redux integration:**\n- File: `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/slices/exploreSlice.ts`\n- Defines `Deal` interface with all above fields\n- Creates `fetchExploreDeals()` async thunk that calls `/api/explore-deals?origin={originCode}`\n- Manages state: `deals[]`, `dealsLoading` boolean\n\nAll test files follow consistent patterns using Playwright with strong reliance on `data-testid` attributes for element selection, and include proper async/await handling with reasonable timeouts."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a035de66b56126fc7 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 42895\ntool_uses: 20\nduration_ms: 35526</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"070807e6-44c2-402e-bd72-2ebebd488457","uuid":"79ecdc3a-0b4e-4a18-bb96-6af230baa85f","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Find the Google Flights app in the /repo/apps directory. I need to:\n1. Find the app directory name\n2. Find the DealsSection component and read it\n3. Find docs/tests.md in the app and read the entries related to DealsSection\n4. Find the playwright config file\n5. Find any existing test files to understand the test patterns used\n6. Find the Explore page component that uses DealsSection\n7. Find any Netlify functions related to deals\n\nBe thorough - read the full contents of all relevant files.","agentId":"a035de66b56126fc7","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me compile all the information I've gathered for you.\n\n## Summary of Findings\n\nI've completed a thorough exploration of the Google Flights app in the `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights` directory. Here's everything you requested:\n\n### 1. App Directory Name\n**Location:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights`\n\n### 2. DealsSection Component\n**File:** `/repo/apps/GoogleFlights/src/components/DealsSection.tsx`\n\nThe component:\n- Takes props: `deals` (Deal[]), `loading` (boolean), `originCode` (string | null)\n- Displays deal cards in a responsive grid with `grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr))`\n- Shows loading state with 4 skeleton cards\n- Shows empty state message when no deals available\n- Each d